Record kernel launches into one command encoder and compute pass, submitted every four
dispatches with one pair of error scopes popped at the next read back or sync. Defer destroying
evicted storage until the batch is submitted, and size the storage cache from peak use.
Keep bind groups and uniform buffers for repeated dispatches. Upload through mapped staging
buffers in 4 MB chunks and read back through one staging buffer the size of the copy, copying
once with Write/ReadMappedRange. Weak hooks let an embedder write host bytes held outside
linear memory.

